### Member CRUD Tests via Project Composition
### Prerequisites: Start the server with `cds watch` or `npm start`

### Variables
@baseUrl = http://localhost:4004
@projectService = {{baseUrl}}/projman

### 1. Create a test project first (Members depend on Projects)
# @name createProject
POST {{projectService}}/Project
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Test Project for Members",
  "description": "A project to test member operations via HTTP",
  "startDate": "2024-01-01",
  "endDate": "2024-12-31",
  "status_ID": 1
}

### 2. Activate the project draft
# @name activateProject
POST {{projectService}}/Project(ID={{createProject.response.body.ID}},IsActiveEntity=false)/draftActivate
Content-Type: application/json

### 3. Edit the project to add members
# @name editProject
POST {{projectService}}/Project(ID={{activateProject.response.body.ID}},IsActiveEntity=true)/draftEdit
Content-Type: application/json

### 4. Create a member via project composition
# @name createMember1
POST {{projectService}}/Project(ID={{editProject.response.body.ID}},IsActiveEntity=false)/team
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "member_userId": "101",
  "role_ID": 1,
  "hasAssignment": false
}

### 5. Create a second member
# @name createMember2
POST {{projectService}}/Project(ID={{editProject.response.body.ID}},IsActiveEntity=false)/team
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "member_userId": "102",
  "role_ID": 2,
  "hasAssignment": true
}

### 6. Create a third member
# @name createMember3
POST {{projectService}}/Project(ID={{editProject.response.body.ID}},IsActiveEntity=false)/team
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "member_userId": "103",
  "role_ID": 7,
  "hasAssignment": false
}

### 7. Activate the draft to save all members
# @name activateMembersProject
POST {{projectService}}/Project(ID={{editProject.response.body.ID}},IsActiveEntity=false)/draftActivate
Content-Type: application/json

### 8. Read project with expanded team members
# @name readProjectWithTeam
GET {{projectService}}/Project(ID={{activateMembersProject.response.body.ID}},IsActiveEntity=true)?$expand=team

### 9. Read project with expanded team and employee details
# @name readProjectWithTeamAndMembers
GET {{projectService}}/Project(ID={{activateMembersProject.response.body.ID}},IsActiveEntity=true)?$expand=team($expand=member)

### 10. Read project with expanded team and role details
# @name readProjectWithTeamAndRoles
GET {{projectService}}/Project(ID={{activateMembersProject.response.body.ID}},IsActiveEntity=true)?$expand=team($expand=role)

### 11. Access specific member via composition path
# @name readSpecificMember
GET {{projectService}}/Project(ID={{activateMembersProject.response.body.ID}},IsActiveEntity=true)/team({{createMember1.response.body.ID}})

### 12. Access member with expanded associations
# @name readMemberWithAssociations
GET {{projectService}}/Project(ID={{activateMembersProject.response.body.ID}},IsActiveEntity=true)/team({{createMember1.response.body.ID}})?$expand=member,role

### 13. Update member through project composition - Edit the project
# @name editProjectForUpdate
POST {{projectService}}/Project(ID={{activateMembersProject.response.body.ID}},IsActiveEntity=true)/draftEdit
Content-Type: application/json

### 14. Update the member
# @name updateMember
PATCH {{projectService}}/Project(ID={{editProjectForUpdate.response.body.ID}},IsActiveEntity=false)/team({{createMember1.response.body.ID}})
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "role_ID": 3,
  "hasAssignment": true
}

### 15. Activate the draft to save changes
# @name activateUpdateProject
POST {{projectService}}/Project(ID={{editProjectForUpdate.response.body.ID}},IsActiveEntity=false)/draftActivate
Content-Type: application/json

### 16. Verify the changes were saved
# @name verifyMemberUpdate
GET {{projectService}}/Project(ID={{activateUpdateProject.response.body.ID}},IsActiveEntity=true)/team({{createMember1.response.body.ID}})

### 17. Update member employee assignment - Edit the project again
# @name editProjectForEmployeeUpdate
POST {{projectService}}/Project(ID={{activateUpdateProject.response.body.ID}},IsActiveEntity=true)/draftEdit
Content-Type: application/json

### 18. Change the employee assigned to this member
# @name updateMemberEmployee
PATCH {{projectService}}/Project(ID={{editProjectForEmployeeUpdate.response.body.ID}},IsActiveEntity=false)/team({{createMember1.response.body.ID}})
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "member_userId": "102"
}

### 19. Activate the draft
# @name activateEmployeeUpdateProject
POST {{projectService}}/Project(ID={{editProjectForEmployeeUpdate.response.body.ID}},IsActiveEntity=false)/draftActivate
Content-Type: application/json

### 20. Verify the employee change
# @name verifyEmployeeChange
GET {{projectService}}/Project(ID={{activateEmployeeUpdateProject.response.body.ID}},IsActiveEntity=true)/team({{createMember1.response.body.ID}})?$expand=member

### 21. Filter team members by role
# @name filterByRole
GET {{projectService}}/Project(ID={{activateEmployeeUpdateProject.response.body.ID}},IsActiveEntity=true)?$expand=team($filter=role_ID eq 2)

### 22. Filter team members by assignment status
# @name filterByAssignmentStatus
GET {{projectService}}/Project(ID={{activateEmployeeUpdateProject.response.body.ID}},IsActiveEntity=true)?$expand=team($filter=hasAssignment eq true)

### 23. Filter team members by employee
# @name filterByEmployee
GET {{projectService}}/Project(ID={{activateEmployeeUpdateProject.response.body.ID}},IsActiveEntity=true)?$expand=team($filter=member_userId eq '102')

### 24. Delete member through project composition - Edit the project
# @name editProjectForDeletion
POST {{projectService}}/Project(ID={{activateEmployeeUpdateProject.response.body.ID}},IsActiveEntity=true)/draftEdit
Content-Type: application/json

### 25. Delete a specific member (deleting createMember3)
# @name deleteMember
DELETE {{projectService}}/Project(ID={{editProjectForDeletion.response.body.ID}},IsActiveEntity=false)/team({{createMember3.response.body.ID}})

### 26. Activate the draft to save deletion
# @name activateDeletionProject
POST {{projectService}}/Project(ID={{editProjectForDeletion.response.body.ID}},IsActiveEntity=false)/draftActivate
Content-Type: application/json

### 27. Verify the member was deleted
# @name verifyDeletion
GET {{projectService}}/Project(ID={{activateDeletionProject.response.body.ID}},IsActiveEntity=true)?$expand=team

### 28. Test Member Service Entity Direct Access
# @name listAllMembers
GET {{projectService}}/Member

### 29. Read member with projected member_name
# @name readMemberProjection
GET {{projectService}}/Member?$select=ID,member_userId,member_name,role_ID,hasAssignment

### 30. Filter members by project via Member service
# @name filterMembersByProject
GET {{projectService}}/Member?$filter=parent_ID eq '{{activateDeletionProject.response.body.ID}}'

### 31. Test error cases - Edit the project for error testing
# @name editProjectForErrorTest
POST {{projectService}}/Project(ID={{activateDeletionProject.response.body.ID}},IsActiveEntity=true)/draftEdit
Content-Type: application/json

### 32. Create member with non-existent employee (should fail)
# @name createMemberInvalidEmployee
POST {{projectService}}/Project(ID={{editProjectForErrorTest.response.body.ID}},IsActiveEntity=false)/team
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "member_userId": "999999",
  "role_ID": 1,
  "hasAssignment": false
}

### 33. Test error cases - Try to create member with invalid role
# @name createMemberInvalidRole
POST {{projectService}}/Project(ID={{editProjectForErrorTest.response.body.ID}},IsActiveEntity=false)/team
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "member_userId": "101",
  "role_ID": 999,
  "hasAssignment": false
}

### 34. Clean up - Delete the test project (this will cascade delete members)
# @name cleanupProject
DELETE {{projectService}}/Project(ID={{activateDeletionProject.response.body.ID}},IsActiveEntity=true)

### 35. Verify cleanup
# @name verifyCleanup
GET {{projectService}}/Project(ID={{activateDeletionProject.response.body.ID}},IsActiveEntity=true)

### Additional helpful queries for debugging

### List all projects
GET {{projectService}}/Project

### List all roles
GET {{projectService}}/Role

### List all employees
GET {{projectService}}/Employee
